  "body": "The maintainer reported this bug in chat on 2026-11-17, on the 0.23.0 build:\n\n> Bug; the machine list is not updated from foloder on start. Neither is it updated when refreshed. It instead just errors over not finding the file it needs.. When the files is actually removedd..\n\nWhat happens:\n- At start, the machine list does not show the contents of the machine folder (`assets`, read at run time since #2282, PR #2293).\n- A refresh does not update the list.\n- When a machine file is removed from the folder, the list still has its entry. The program then gives an error that it cannot find the file.\n\nExpected:\n- At start and at each refresh, the list has one entry for each machine file that is in the folder at that moment.\n- A file that is removed from the folder has no entry after the start or the refresh. No error shows for it.\n- A file that is added to the folder has an entry after the start or the refresh.\n- A missing file that the open document or the default machine needs is still refused by name (#2319). This rule does not change.\n\nNot known yet:\n- If the list comes from a fixed table in the program and not from a scan of the folder.\n- Which control the maintainer used for the refresh.\n- If MCP has the same list. If it does, it must follow the same scan.\n\nRelated: #2358 (list the user's machines in the Machine library list) is an enhancement and is a different change.\n\nDone means: a test adds a machine file to a temporary machine folder and removes a different file, then starts or refreshes. The list has the added machine, does not have the removed machine, and shows no error.\n",
